<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minoan civilisation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 3000–1100 BCE</span> · Also known as Minoans, Minoan civilization</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Minoan civilisation was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> civilisation on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, named by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-evans">Arthur Evans</a> after the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minos">King Minos</a>. From about 2000 BCE it built great palace complexes at Knossos, Phaistos, Malia and Zakros, used the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linear-a">Linear A</a> script and traded widely across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> and the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. After about 1450 BCE Crete came under Mycenaean Greek rule, and the palaces were destroyed or abandoned.</p></div>
